{title: Rescue the Perishing}
{artist: Fanny Crosby / William H. Doane}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: F}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Rescue the perishing, care for the dying
[C7]Snatch them in pity from sin and the [F]grave
Weep o'er the erring one, lift up the fallen
[C7]Tell them of Jesus, the mighty to [F]save
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Rescue the perishing, care for the dying
[Bb]Jesus is merciful, [C7]Jesus will [F]save
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Though they are slighting Him, still He is waiting
[C7]Waiting the penitent child to re[F]ceive
Plead with them earnestly, plead with them gently
[C7]He will forgive if they only be[F]lieve
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Down in the human heart, crushed by the tempter
[C7]Feelings lie buried that grace can re[F]store
Touched by a loving heart, wakened by kindness
[C7]Chords that were broken will vibrate once [F]more
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Rescue the perishing, duty demands it
[C7]Strength for thy labor the Lord will pro[F]vide
Back to the narrow way patiently win them
[C7]Tell the poor wanderer a Saviour has [F]died
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
